course: dictionary
lesson: 5253
title: Joining: putting things together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Joining is the -ing form of the verb join. To join means to put things together, or to become part of a group. So joining can mean adding pieces together, or becoming a member of a club or team.
explain: Context shows which meaning the writer means. «In a joining story we know two of three numbers: how many at first, how many came, how many at the end.» Here joining means putting numbers together, so you use the two numbers you know to find the third.
explain: Joining can also mean taking part. When you are joining in a game, you are not just watching: you are one of the players. Ask yourself: is something being put together, or is someone becoming part of a group? Either way, joining means connecting.
fact: Joining is the -ing form of join.
fact: Joining can be a verb, as in «joining a club», or a noun, meaning the act of putting together.
fact: «Joining in» means taking part in an activity with other people.
fact: In joined-up writing, the letters of a word are linked together.
fact: In maths, joining two points with a line draws a shape.
exercise: «She is joining the swimming club on Monday.» What does joining mean here? | Painting the club sign | *Becoming a member of the club | Swimming very fast | Leaving the club for good
exercise: «Come and join in our game!» What does join in mean? | Watch from the side | Clean up the playground | *Take part with the others | Go home early
exercise: «In a joining story we know two of three numbers: how many at first, how many came, how many at the end.» In this story, what does joining mean? | Writing numbers in joined-up writing | *Putting parts together to find the whole | Taking numbers away | Counting backwards only
test: What is linked together in joined-up writing? | *The letters of a word | The pages of a book | The pencils in a pot
test: A joining fee is paid when you do what? | Finish a book | Lose a game | Leave a club | *Become a member of a club
exam: Which sentence uses joining as a noun, meaning the act of putting together? | She is joining her friends at the park | *The joining of the two pipes took a long time | They are joining the queue now
